  "term": "friendship",
  "definition": "Friendship is a relationship in which two or more people feel mutual affection or goodwill and want one another’s company. In its stricter sense, it involves reciprocity, some depth of feeling, and a willingness to help each other, usually with some harmony or complementarity of character.",
